Experiment 3: Implement Queue using Stacks (Leetcode Problem 232)

Aim:Implement a First In First Out (FIFO) queue using only two stacks. The implemented queue should support push, pop, peek, and empty operations.

Algorithm:

1.) Start
2.) Create two stacks s1 and s2.
3.) For the push(x) operation:
Move all elements from s1 to s2.
Push the new element x into s1.
Move all elements back from s2 to s1.
4.) For the pop() operation:
Remove the top element of s1 and return it.
5.) For the peek() operation:
Return the top element of s1 without removing it.
6.) For the empty() operation:
Check whether s1 is empty.
Return true if it is empty; otherwise, return false.
7.) End

Code:
class MyQueue {
public:
    stack<int> s1;
    stack<int> s2;

    MyQueue() {

    }

    void push(int x) {
        while(!s1.empty()){
            s2.push(s1.top());
            s1.pop();
        }
        s1.push(x);
        while(!s2.empty()){
            s1.push(s2.top());
            s2.pop();
        }
    }

    int pop() {
        int x=s1.top();
        s1.pop();
        return x;
    }

    int peek() {
        return s1.top();
    }

    bool empty() {
        return s1.empty();
    }
};
